{
 "points": [
  {
   "id": "P1.1",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Hyperparameters tuned per concept and task on reported metric, undercutting minimal-tuning claim.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.2",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Baselines use recommended configs without comparable per-concept tuning.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.3",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "No held-out selection or joint hyperparameter sensitivity analysis.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.4",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Mask-construction and evaluation prompts may overlap.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.5",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "No evaluation on paraphrases, synonyms or compositional prompts.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.6",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Classifier forgetting accuracy ignores residual visual traces.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.7",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Style metrics CLIPa and FSR conflate removal with degradation; no classifier or human study.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.8",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Preservation of related neighbouring concepts not checked.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.9",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Quality-preservation claim overstated given CLIP drop.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.10",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "FID not reported for Imagenette.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.11",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Reported numbers internally inconsistent across tables.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.12",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Zero standard deviations suspicious.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.13",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Seeds, images per class and runs unstated; no significance tests.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.14",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Some baseline numbers copied from prior papers; SD versions mixed.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.15",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Average rank hides weaknesses on FID and CLIP.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.16",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Eq. 1 cosine term is heuristic without theory or ablation.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.17",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Eq. 2 is not a significance test; statistical significance claim unjustified.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.18",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Retaining neurons shared by many concepts may leak concepts.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.19",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Saliency may capture generic high-norm weights.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.20",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Ablations only on Imagenette.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.21",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Adversarial attacks still recover erased content in most cases.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.22",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Arrows in Table 15 unexplained.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.23",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "No tests of recovery via fine-tuning, inversion or probing.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.24",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Explicit-content experiments narrow: two words, single NudeNet threshold.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.25",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Limited novelty over ConceptPrune; first-work claim rests on narrow reading.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.26",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "No ablation isolating saliency score versus fusion pipeline.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.27",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Related-work citation errors and misdescriptions.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.28",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Only SD v1.4/1.5; no SDXL, SD3 or DiT models.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.29",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Code not released.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.30",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Concept-scaling claims depend on arbitrary thresholds and classifier-friendly classes.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
